# {{NAME}}

An external oveRTOS application (Rust).

## Build

```bash
make host.posix.{{CONFIG_NAME}}     # POSIX host
make qemu.freertos.{{CONFIG_NAME}}  # QEMU + FreeRTOS

make            # download, configure, build
make run        # launch (POSIX) or boot in QEMU
```

`OVE_DIR` is set in `Makefile`. Override per invocation:

```bash
make OVE_DIR=/other/path/to/oveRTOS host.posix.{{CONFIG_NAME}} && make
```

## Layout

```
{{NAME}}/
├── Makefile         # delegates to $(OVE_DIR)/config/make/ove_app.mk
├── app.yaml         # manifest
├── Cargo.toml       # Rust dependencies
├── build.rs         # build script (oveRTOS bindings driven by its own build.rs)
├── src/lib.rs       # entry — ove::main!(app_main)
└── output/          # generated workspace
```

## Allocator

The template links `ove-allocator` which registers a libc-malloc-backed `#[global_allocator]` on bare-metal targets. On `std` builds (POSIX), the install is suppressed via the `no_install` feature so it doesn't conflict with the std allocator.

